WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.520 --> 00:00:04.640
There are definitely elements in Shazam! that
kids might simply blow right past on their

00:00:04.640 --> 00:00:08.820
way to experiencing the superhero spectacle
and the heart of the family story, while adult

00:00:08.820 --> 00:00:11.860
superhero fans are still turning those ideas
over in their heads.

00:00:11.900 --> 00:00:15.640
Here's some stuff in Shazam! that you might
only notice if you're an adult.

00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:20.740
Shazam! takes place in the same world as Man
of Steel, Justice League, and the other recent

00:00:20.740 --> 00:00:26.490
DC movies, which means Batman, Superman, Wonder
Woman, and Aquaman exist alongside Billy Batson

00:00:26.490 --> 00:00:27.480
and Freddy Freeman.

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:31.900
That's probably why Freddy is absolutely obsessed
with those super-people, but it seems he's

00:00:31.900 --> 00:00:32.940
not the only one.

00:00:33.240 --> 00:00:37.440
As we see from Freddy's collection of memorabilia
and a chase scene through a toy store, this

00:00:37.440 --> 00:00:41.720
world has reacted to superheroes in the same
way that ours has: merchandising!

00:00:41.720 --> 00:00:42.760
“ Merchandising!

00:00:42.980 --> 00:00:44.080
Merchandising!

00:00:44.640 --> 00:00:46.840
Where the real money from the movie is made!”

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:53.180
Yes, Batman and Superman are real, and they
have their own action figures, replica weaponry,

00:00:53.190 --> 00:00:55.170
and even t-shirts, just like we have.

00:00:55.170 --> 00:00:57.680
So how exactly does that work in the world
of the film?

00:00:57.890 --> 00:01:01.700
Those heroes all have secret identities, so
did those companies get permission to use

00:01:01.710 --> 00:01:02.710
their likenesses?

00:01:02.710 --> 00:01:04.250
Do the heroes just ignore it?

00:01:04.250 --> 00:01:08.389
Bruce Wayne might not need any of the royalties
from his action figures, but you know Aquaman

00:01:08.389 --> 00:01:10.900
would absolutely take a check for his t-shirt
sales.

00:01:11.460 --> 00:01:16.939
The film begins in 1974, when a young Thaddeus
Sivana is brought before the wizard Shazam,

00:01:16.940 --> 00:01:20.760
only to be told he's not worthy because he
was tempted by the Seven Deadly Sins.

00:01:20.840 --> 00:01:25.200
As soon as Sivana leaves, Shazam sends out
a summoning spell to find a champion as quickly

00:01:25.200 --> 00:01:28.060
as possible… which takes about 45 years.

00:01:28.180 --> 00:01:32.380
When Shazam meets Billy, he explains that
they chose a champion once who betrayed them

00:01:32.440 --> 00:01:37.020
someone DC fans will recognize as Black Adam
and that he's been looking for a replacement

00:01:37.040 --> 00:01:37.820
ever since.

00:01:38.040 --> 00:01:42.099
And yet, the wizard has gone through dozens
of potential champions, only to wind up telling

00:01:42.100 --> 00:01:43.380
them all they're not worthy.

00:01:43.580 --> 00:01:44.760
So what took so long?

00:01:44.880 --> 00:01:48.660
There are obviously heroes in the world, and
good and decent people willing to do things

00:01:48.680 --> 00:01:51.360
like, for example, open up their home to foster
kids.

00:01:51.590 --> 00:01:54.980
It's implied that Billy was something of a
compromise because the wizard was running

00:01:54.990 --> 00:01:59.509
out of time, but he probably could've compromised
a little sooner especially when you consider

00:01:59.509 --> 00:02:03.439
that later in the movie, Billy starts handing
out powers to his foster siblings?

00:02:03.439 --> 00:02:08.470
For a guy facing a ticking clock that ran
from ancient Egypt until 2019, he really put

00:02:08.470 --> 00:02:10.619
things off until the last possible moment.

00:02:10.619 --> 00:02:14.000
And he still had to settle for a teenager
who charges for selfies.

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:18.400
"Did you check … typically give me a little
money…"

00:02:19.590 --> 00:02:23.360
Billy Batson is a 14-year-old boy when we
meet him, and when a wizard gives him the

00:02:23.360 --> 00:02:28.600
ability to transform into a full-grown man
simply by saying a magic word, his brain definitely

00:02:28.600 --> 00:02:29.680
stays 14.

00:02:29.970 --> 00:02:34.080
Billy's more than happy to use his newfound
stature to do some very adult things, including

00:02:34.090 --> 00:02:38.800
buying beer which he winds up hating and even
going to a strip club, where he quickly unloads

00:02:38.800 --> 00:02:39.800
all of his cash.

00:02:40.080 --> 00:02:41.080
"We're gonna need more cash.”

00:02:41.080 --> 00:02:42.660
“Why you were in there for like 5 minutes…”

00:02:42.660 --> 00:02:44.170
“Dude they were very convincing!"

00:02:44.620 --> 00:02:49.040
This is generally pretty understandable and
amusing behavior that most 14-year-olds would

00:02:49.041 --> 00:02:52.510
attempt in some form if they thought they
could get away with it, but it also makes

00:02:52.510 --> 00:02:54.500
us wonder how far Billy would have gone.

00:02:54.500 --> 00:02:57.812
If the supervillain threat hadn't grabbed
his attention, would he have tried to buy

00:02:57.812 --> 00:03:01.580
hard liquor, gotten a driver's license, applied
for a low-interest home loan?

00:03:01.580 --> 00:03:05.830
Would he have even moved on from strip clubs
to… well, do we have to say it?

00:03:05.830 --> 00:03:09.760
The film never takes this any further, for
good reason, but it definitely raises the

00:03:09.760 --> 00:03:13.040
question, especially for the people in the
audience who remember what it was like to

00:03:13.040 --> 00:03:14.520
be 14 themselves.

00:03:15.320 --> 00:03:18.820
At the climax of the movie, after learning
what it means to be a hero, Billy shares his

00:03:18.820 --> 00:03:22.560
power with his siblings to create a whole
family of lightning-powered heroes.

00:03:22.840 --> 00:03:28.120
"Guys, I don't believe in violence but I think
we should kick this guys butt like really

00:03:28.120 --> 00:03:28.620
hard."

00:03:29.060 --> 00:03:32.740
That means that all of Billy's foster siblings
will have access to the Rock of Eternity,

00:03:32.740 --> 00:03:36.020
where the Seven Deadly Sins are re-imprisoned
at the end of the film.

00:03:36.200 --> 00:03:40.120
Given that Billy's first impulses hit everything
from lust to gluttony, how do we know that

00:03:40.120 --> 00:03:43.160
one of the younger kids won't one day be tempted
by their power?

00:03:43.240 --> 00:03:46.630
Sounds like things were getting more than
a little desperate if the wizard was willing

00:03:46.630 --> 00:03:47.820
to take that chance.

00:03:48.520 --> 00:03:52.340
The act of selflessness that gets Billy on
the wizard's radar in the first place comes

00:03:52.350 --> 00:03:56.180
when two bullies start beating up Freddy Freeman
after hitting him with their truck.

00:03:56.180 --> 00:03:59.740
They only clip him, and it's not clear if
they meant to do it or if it was just a happy

00:03:59.740 --> 00:04:03.640
accident, but that's the first thing we ever
see them do, and we never really learn anything

00:04:03.640 --> 00:04:04.540
else about them.

00:04:04.640 --> 00:04:07.780
All of the adults out there who have been
through high school themselves are definitely

00:04:07.780 --> 00:04:12.840
aware that, sometimes, kids can be jerks for
no good reason and get away with it but still.

00:04:13.010 --> 00:04:17.400
Constantly picking on a disabled classmate
to the point of running him over with a truck?

00:04:17.420 --> 00:04:20.180
Even the crappiest school would have a pretty
big problem with that.

00:04:20.350 --> 00:04:23.180
The film never shows us anything that hints
at their motivation.

00:04:23.180 --> 00:04:27.040
So if that's just how they are, maybe they
should be in prison instead of high school.

00:04:27.780 --> 00:04:32.020
Though Shazam is also simply the name of the
wizard in the film, we are given a more detailed

00:04:32.020 --> 00:04:36.800
reason why Billy needs to say that exact word:
It's an acrostic, and by saying it, the champion

00:04:36.800 --> 00:04:41.039
is imbued with the wisdom of Solomon, the
strength of Hercules, the endurance of Atlas,

00:04:41.040 --> 00:04:44.500
the power of Zeus, the courage of Achilles,
and the speed of Mercury.

00:04:44.689 --> 00:04:48.180
Throughout the course of the film, we see
Billy ultimately using all of these abilities

00:04:48.180 --> 00:04:50.540
except one: the Wisdom of Solomon.

00:04:51.060 --> 00:04:52.140
"How do I know my name?

00:04:52.340 --> 00:04:57.200
Ah… how do I know your name…? one of my
super-powers is name-guessing."

00:04:58.020 --> 00:05:02.180
Billy's still a teenage boy, so we can't expect
that wisdom to be in action all the time,

00:05:02.180 --> 00:05:06.380
but the wizard explains he will possess this
wisdom and then we never really see it.

00:05:06.380 --> 00:05:09.820
You'd think he could have at least put it
to good use to ace a math test or something.

00:05:10.120 --> 00:05:14.740
The film does a good job of contrasting Billy's
superhero abilities with his teenage fallibility,

00:05:14.740 --> 00:05:18.789
and maybe we'll get to see a little more of
that problem-solving in future films.

00:05:18.789 --> 00:05:21.900
With a mind-controlling worm showing up, he'll
probably need it.

